N:game-design-theory
D:Turn one game-design question into a falsifiable theory packet. Choose one bounded lens, separate evidence from assumption, map mechanic to dynamic to experience, name counterevidence, compare one reversible variant, validate game-design-hypothesis.json, and route production or implementation outward.
G:game-design-theory MDA mechanics-dynamics-aesthetics player-motivation core-loop design-hypothesis reward-loop resource-flow dominant-strategy mastery autonomy competence relatedness playtest

U[8]:
  Trace mechanics through runtime dynamics to intended or observed player experience
  Explain weak confusing dominant shallow or conflicting game systems
  Analyze core loops choices uncertainty progression rewards resources and mastery
  Frame autonomy competence and relatedness as context-specific motivation hypotheses
  Reconcile conflicting playtest observations without averaging away barriers
  Compare a control and one reversible design variant
  Define counterevidence and the smallest prototype that can change a design belief
  Validate game-design-hypothesis.json before routing into production

S[8]{n,step,details}:
  1,Freeze one question,Name the observed behavior evidence context controllable variable unlocked decision and out-of-scope surfaces
  2,Choose one primary lens,Use MDA motivation needs decision structure feedback/resource loops or learning/mastery; add a secondary lens only when it changes the experiment
  3,Build the causal chain,Map mechanic -> interaction -> runtime dynamic -> perceived signal -> experience and mark every unsupported arrow as an assumption
  4,State the falsifier,Record expected signal competing explanation counterevidence and unchanged factors before building the variant
  5,Design one comparison,Prefer a reversible prototype or data/config change; keep control and variant identical except for the intended variable
  6,Collect bounded evidence,Use target context and pair behavioral with qualitative evidence; do not invent universal sample sizes ratios or engagement targets
  7,Interpret conservatively,Report observations before explanations and inspect implementation exposure learning order familiarity accessibility and confounds
  8,Validate and route,Run validate-design-hypothesis.py; return keep revise reject or inconclusive; route production feel UI balance telemetry and engine work to their owners

R[9]:
  Theory is a lens for a testable claim not a universal recipe for fun
  One primary lens is required and its blind spots must be stated
  MDA distinguishes mechanics runtime dynamics and player aesthetics but one dynamic can be interpreted differently
  Autonomy competence and relatedness are hypotheses in a context not required checklist items
  Bartle types are not universal player segments and stay limited to relevant evidenced multiplayer contexts
  Retention session length and spend alone do not prove a desired experience
  Every hypothesis names counterevidence before the prototype runs
  Numeric thresholds sample sizes curves and ratios require project-owned risk and population evidence
  Full GDD and production work route to bmad-gds or game-studio-harness

E[4]{type,command}:
  Install skill,npx skills add https://github.com/akillness/jeo-skills --skill game-design-theory
  Validate example,python3 .agent-skills/game-design-theory/scripts/validate-design-hypothesis.py .agent-skills/game-design-theory/references/hypothesis-example.json
  Self-test validator,python3 .agent-skills/game-design-theory/scripts/validate-design-hypothesis.py --self-test
  Validate skill,bash .agent-skills/skill-standardization/scripts/validate_skill.sh .agent-skills/game-design-theory
